<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sikh Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Lahore Darbar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sikh Empire was a state in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a> founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranjit-singh">Maharaja Ranjit Singh</a> at the start of the nineteenth century, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lahore">Lahore</a>. It extended to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashmir">Kashmir</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/multan">Multan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peshawar">Peshawar</a> and maintained a powerful, partly Western-trained army. After Ranjit Singh's death in 1839 it fell into factional turmoil and was annexed by the British after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-anglo-sikh-war">Second Anglo-Sikh War</a> of 1848–1849.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sikh-empire.jpg" alt="Sikh Empire" width="320" height="246" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AfghanTsakhtan · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Sikh_Empire.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
